%% Realtime, never polling — full flow
%% Pure Mermaid. No Markdown fence around this file.

flowchart TD
    trigger([A screen shows data that changes after first render,<br/>or code holds a timer near a fetch]) --> kind{What is being waited for?}

    kind -->|a moment in time| clock[Server returns the timestamp<br/>a local timer flips the UI<br/>no request]
    kind -->|new work for a worker| kick[Kick on enqueue:<br/>trigger to pg_net, DB webhook, queue consumer<br/>cron only for timed work]
    kind -->|data that changes| source{Who can tell us it changed?}

    source -->|our database| db{Hot table or<br/>~3,000+ subscribers?}
    db -->|no| pgc[postgres_changes<br/>filter the policy can prove]
    db -->|yes| bcast[Broadcast from the database<br/>private topic + realtime.messages policy]
    source -->|a provider| hook[Signed webhook into our DB<br/>then the database path]
    hook --> db
    source -->|our own server| sse[SSE or WebSocket]
    source -->|another runtime| plat[Extension messaging, Flutter streams,<br/>Firestore onSnapshot, Laravel Echo, Tauri events]

    pgc --> client
    bcast --> client
    sse --> client
    plat --> client

    client[Client pattern:<br/>event = signal, debounced re-read<br/>re-read on SUBSCRIBED, focus, online, visible<br/>own the channel, backoff resubscribe<br/>bounded filter, switch-gated]

    kind -->|nothing can push it| exc{One of the four exceptions?<br/>no-push-remote, platform-no-connection,<br/>local-timer, test-wait}
    exc -->|no| bug[It is a polling bug:<br/>find a push source]
    bug --> source
    exc -->|yes| mark[Mark the line<br/>// polling-exception: kind — reason<br/>server or CLI only, backoff, ceiling, terminal stop]

    clock --> gate
    kick --> gate
    client --> gate
    mark --> gate

    gate[Gate: ESLint no-restricted-syntax<br/>or a ratchet verify step] --> prove{Four proofs pass?<br/>latency under 2 s, idle network 0 requests,<br/>offline gap closes, plant fails}
    prove -->|no| fix[Fix the source or the lifecycle] --> prove
    prove -->|yes| done([Done: pushed, bounded, proved])
